				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2902864&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607633170" alt="MaliceAforethought" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2902864)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/maliceaforethought" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2902864); return false;" >MaliceAforethought</a></span> <span class="odate time_1522776990 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">03 Apr 2018 17:36</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3758163">
									

<p>Ah, hmm. I guess I do have a tendency to overdo the crosslinks a little; rest assured that none of them are actually integral to understanding the article. My reasoning is as follows:</p>
<ul>
<li>&quot;as per the <a href="/scp-3466">Boring Agreement</a>&quot; &#8212; this one is probably the <em>most</em> necessary of them, because it provides a link for users who don't know the WWS background. The nature of the agreement can be gotten from context (at least, I hope so), but I wanted to direct some attention to the scip that started it all.</li>
<li>&quot;Class-E (&quot;<a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-5174970#post-3701841">Momentary Lapse of Reason</a>&quot;) wormholes&quot; &#8212; this, I suppose, isn't really necessary. It's pretty clear from context, and would probably be better linked in the discussion page. Consider it changed.</li>
<li>&quot;the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/nexus-series">Asphodel-class</a> nexus&quot; &#8212; same as before, really. It's not actually important, and I guess I could remove it without harming the flow of the article too much. On the other hand, the nexuses page is one I think deserves more attention, so the argument <em>for</em> this one is that I want to facilitate more interesting wiki-walks.</li>
<li>&quot;Mobile Task Force Beta-4 (&quot;<a href="/scp-3577">Castaways</a>&quot;)&quot; &#8212; yeah, okay. I used weryllium's task force and wanted to give credit, but I guess an actual crosslink is a little gratuitous here. This one can probably go.</li>
<li>&quot;the Foundation's <a href="/multi-u-101">Department of Extra-Universal Affairs</a>&quot; &#8212; I really want to keep this one. The Multi-U tales were a big part of what got me wanting to write this in the first place, and I'd much prefer giving them a mention in the article.</li>
</ul>
<p>So yeah. I guess I did go a little overboard, huh. Hopefully I've cleared it up a little, and if you have any suggestions I'd love to hear them (it was probably a mistake to tie together so many different bits of canon in such a small article). Thanks for reading in any case.</p>

							</div>

								
					
